{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_5fc10695-482b-4eba-a36c-58fb17ea46ba","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_b431dfe2c98c7887","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/qiba/ROCm.AI/hyperloom/session/Ornith-1.5-397B-FP8/20260915T161838Z-ba2694ea/runs/specialist/fc07edbde4c9489682f2cafa5a7d253a/specialist_done.json","content":"{\n  \"intent_type\": \"specialist_done\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"confidence\": 0.82,\n    \"domain\": \"enablement_specialist\",\n    \"empty\": false,\n    \"gap_canonical_id\": \"gap.enablement.unknown\",\n    \"summary\": \"Diagnosed the CURRENT (deeper) boot failure as a stale vLLM torch.compile AOT cache, NOT a new code gap. The kept FP8-emulation patch (001) edits only UNTRACED files (kernel registry __init__.py + new scaled_mm/emulation.py), so vllm/compilation/caching.py keeps the same cache key and reloads the pre-patch artifact (torch_aot_compile/63eba2e.../rank_*_0/model, mtime 15:13, built for FP8 [K,N] aten._scaled_mm). Replaying that graph against the now-BF16 [N,K] dequantized weight dies in profile_run: assert_size_stride arg10_1 (4096,2560)/(1,4096) vs actual (2560,4096)/(4096,1). VERIFIED ON MY CARDS: booting the 001-patched tree with a fresh compile cache clears profile_run, allocates KV cache, captures CUDA graphs, and serves coherent tokens (17*23->391; correct 'sky is blue' reasoning). Authored patch 002 to make this structural: it folds a digest of model_executor/kernels + layers/quantization + layers/fused_moe/oracle into aot_compile_hash_factors so any kernel-selection patch invalidates the cache and forces a correct recompile. This is expected to clear the gap to FULL runnability for Ornith-1.5-397B-FP8 / vllm / MI250X.\",\n    \"new_findings\": [\n      {\n        \"what\": \"vLLM 0.28 AOT compile-cache invalidation gap: envs.compile_factors() + VllmConfig.compute_hash() + _model_hash_key(forward) form the artifact dir key, and caching._verify_source_unchanged only re-checks the TRACED files recorded inside the EXISTING artifact. A kernel-selection patch (swap which linear/MoE kernel is chosen, changing weight layout/dtype) touches files that were NEVER in the traced set, so the stale artifact still verifies and is silently replayed -> wrong-shape assert_size_stride in profile_run even though the eager path is correct. Kernel-enablement patches therefore REQUIRE a cold compile.\",\n        \"source\": \"/opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/compilation/caching.py:573-620 (aot_compile_hash_factors/_verify_source_unchanged), decorators.py:560-575 (load path), /root/.cache/vllm/torch_compile_cache/torch_aot_compile/63eba2e.../rank_0_0/model (mtime 15:13, pre-17:03 patched run), integrate_patch server.log assert_size_stride arg10_1\",\n        \"expected_impact\": \"Unblocks the full enablement ladder for FP8-emulation combos on pre-MI300 ROCm: with the key invalidated the graph is re-traced against the dequantized BF16 weights, profile_run completes, CUDA graphs capture, and the server serves.\",\n        \"accuracy_risk\": \"none (pure build-cache correctness; the recompiled graph is semantically identical to the correct eager path)\",\n        \"domain_tags\": [\"vllm\", \"torch.compile\", \"aot-cache-invalidation\", \"fp8-emulation\", \"enablement\", \"gfx90a\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"what\": \"End-to-end runnability evidence for Ornith-1.5-397B-FP8 (Qwen3_5MoeForConditionalGeneration, 60-layer hybrid GDN+full-attn, 512-expert MoE, compressed-tensors FP8 w8a8 channel/token) on 8xMI250X TP8: model load 48.3 GiB/GPU (~4% VRAM headroom after ~0.59 GiB BF16 dense dequant), cold torch.compile ~127 s, KV cache 3.48 GiB / 154,624 tokens, both PIECEWISE(51) and FULL(35) CUDA graph capture complete, Application startup, and coherent greedy generations. MoE FP8 path runs with VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=0 (triton/emulated experts) without error.\",\n        \"source\": \"verify_server.log (this dispatch: patched worktree + fresh VLLM_CACHE_ROOT, TP8, gpu_mem_util 0.95, max_model_len 6144)\",\n        \"expected_impact\": \"Confirms the gap closes to a runnable, graph-captured server (not just one boot step). Coordinator's E2E gate should now pass runnability.\",\n        \"accuracy_risk\": \"low; dense FP8 linears dequantize exactly (E4M3->BF16) and activations stay BF16, so quality is >= true w8a8. 4% VRAM headroom is tight at concurrency 64 / 6144 ctx.\",\n        \"domain_tags\": [\"vllm\", \"mi250x\", \"qwen3_5_moe\", \"enablement\", \"runnability\"]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"patches_written\": [\n      \"patches/002_kernel_selection_invalidates_aot_cache.patch\"\n    ],\n    \"artifacts_written\": [],\n    \"setup_commands\": [],\n    \"proposal_set\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"cold-compile-fallback-no-cache\",\n        \"args_mode\": \"append\",\n        \"atomic\": false,\n        \"extra_args\": \"\",\n        \"extra_envs\": {\n          \"VLLM_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE\": \"1\"\n        },\n        \"kb_evidence\": [],\n        \"pr_evidence\": [],\n        \"source_evidence\": [\n          \"vllm/compilation/decorators.py:564 (load skipped when VLLM_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE=1)\",\n          \"vllm/compilation/decorators.py:689 (save skipped when VLLM_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE=1)\",\n          \"verify_server.log: fresh-cache boot of the 001-patched tree cleared profile_run, captured CUDA graphs, served coherent tokens\"\n        ],\n        \"reason\": \"Patch-free fallback that independently clears the CURRENT (stale-AOT-cache) failure: forcing a cold compile guarantees the pre-patch FP8-layout graph (built before patch 001) is never reloaded, so the dequantized BF16 weights are traced correctly. Use if patch 002 cannot be applied or a poisoned artifact would otherwise share the new key. Cost: ~127 s extra cold compile on warm start (irrelevant here since the baseline never booted, so no valid throughput baseline exists yet).\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"patched-tree-fresh-cache-root\",\n        \"args_mode\": \"append\",\n        \"atomic\": false,\n        \"extra_args\": \"\",\n        \"extra_envs\": {\n          \"VLLM_CACHE_ROOT\": \"/home/qiba/ROCm.AI/hyperloom/.cache/vllm_ornith397b_enable\"\n        },\n        \"kb_evidence\": [],\n        \"pr_evidence\": [],\n        \"source_evidence\": [\n          \"vllm/envs.py:2229 (VLLM_CACHE_ROOT is in compile_factors() ignored_factors, i.e. relocating the root does NOT change the AOT hash -> guarantees the existing poisoned 63eba2e... artifact is bypassed)\",\n          \"vllm/compilation/decorators.py:544-563 (aot_compilation_path derived from envs.VLLM_CACHE_ROOT)\"\n        ],\n        \"reason\": \"Second patch-free fallback: points VLLM's cache root at a fresh, writable directory that does not contain the stale torch_aot_compile/63eba2e... artifact, so the engine cold-compiles against the dequantized weights. Safer than disabling the cache entirely (a correct artifact IS saved for later warm starts). Applies on top of patch 001 (+ optional 002).\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"residual_questions\": [\n      \"If the Coordinator benches patch 002 but a stale artifact under an OLD key still exists, confirm the E2E gate is launched with the patched vllm tree importable (integrate_patch applies against /opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages) so the new cache key takes effect; otherwise prefer proposal cold-compile-fallback-no-cache.\",\n      \"VRAM headroom at gpu_memory_utilization 0.95 is ~4% after the dense FP8->BF16 dequant (+~0.59 GiB/GPU). If concurrency-64 / 6144-ctx eval OOMs at KV allocation, the next rung is lowering a non-expert dense budget or --gpu-memory-utilization, not a code gap.\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n"}}],"model":"qwen3.8-flash-next","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c4cfbc9-eb2f-4f52-bf56